// The sdfmesh package: a signed distance field made into a mesh. A program
// reaches it with 'import sdfmesh', and gets:
//
// - 'surfaceNet', any sdf.Shape made into a manifold 'SurfaceNet' of quads
//   (surface nets, one vertex per piece of surface in a cell, gradient
//   normals, blocks far from the surface skipped), and its 'toMesh' (a
//   mesh.Mesh, each quad cut along its shorter diagonal) and 'toPolyMesh'
//   (a mesh.PolyMesh, for 'validate').
// - 'netLevels', a chain of levels of detail, each meshed from the field.
// - 'GridMesher', the same surface nets on the GPU, of a grid already
//   sampled (sdf's SampleGrid, its samples in a buffer, which a part's own
//   kernel may have written): 'mesh' leaves a 'GridNet' on the GPU, vertex
//   and index buffers a renderer can draw, and 'readBack' makes it a
//   SurfaceNet; 'meshOnTwin' runs the same kernels on the CPU. Bit for bit
//   surfaceNet's dense, unrelaxed net, but for the normals, which come from
//   the grid.
//
// It is a tool, not maths: what it makes is a mesh of a size known only
// once it is made, held in Lists or GPU buffers. The CPU mesher runs on one
// thread. The field it meshes is the sdf package's (the Shape trait, and
// 'gradient' for the normals); what it makes is mesh's Mesh and PolyMesh,
// whose 'meshHash' pins the bits.
//
// It is in two halves, as a package with GPU code is (tools/congo/README.md,
// "A package's gpu/ folder"). src/ is the root module, its files one module,
// and only this one, the root, imports:
//
//   mesher.cone       SurfaceNet, surfaceNet, netLevels, and the tables of a
//                     cell's pieces
//   gridmesher.cone   GridMesher and GridNet: gpu/'s kernels run through
//                     gpuwork, on the GPU or as their twins
//
// gpu/ is the GPU half, compiled into sdfmesh for the CPU as the submodule
// 'gridnet', and for the GPU into sdfmesh.spv:
//
//   gridnet.cone      the kernels (classify, countQuads, scanTotals,
//                     scanApply, gather, place, emit), and divExact and
//                     sqrtExact, IEEE's division and square root made from
//                     integer steps
//
// Importing sdfmesh brings gpuwork and gpu with it, and so SDL3: a program
// that imports it links SDL3.lib, which must be on LIB, and gets SDL3.dll
// beside it, whether it meshes on the GPU or not.

mod sdfmesh;

import libc;
import geomath use *;
import collections use *;
import mesh;
import sdf use *;
import gpu use Device, Buffer, BUFFER_USAGE_STORAGE, BUFFER_USAGE_COPY_DST, BUFFER_USAGE_COPY_SRC,
  BUFFER_USAGE_VERTEX, BUFFER_USAGE_INDEX;
import gpuwork use Kernel, Job, Works, Target, Completion, READ, READ_WRITE, readSpirv, upload, zeroed, runTwin;
// gpu/'s exact arithmetic, for importers (and the tests, which check it
// against the CPU's)
pub use gridnet divExact, sqrtExact;
